      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1790933799506,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "For a standard Transformer block, the parameter count is\ndominated by two parts: self-attention projections and\nthe feed-forward network (FFN).\n\nThe attention projections typically contain four\nmatrices:\n\n\n\n\nso attention has approximately          parameters.\n\nA classic FFN has two linear layers:\n\n\n\nSo again the FFN is around 67%",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "For a standard Transformer block, the parameter count is dominated by two parts: self-attention projections and the feed-forward network (FFN).\n\nThe attention projections typically contain four  matrices:\n\n\n\n\nso attention has approximately          parameters.\n\nA classic FFN has two linear layers:\n\n\n\nSo again the FFN is around 67%",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
