    {
      "id": "-kzjT7z2yThlDogSFgNH3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9006.980839024307,
      "y": 5908.987164170199,
      "width": 1142.461873372396,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#000000",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "PIXeu52qoy5WjsfWXriFD",
        "UlC_tXZiMWwB7C1ushLFa",
        "mEytfiosWFcajHFz-sljr",
        "7-wf0sYz_SXmY0N2ZZYb4"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bBn",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1505368126,
      "version": 993,
      "versionNonce": 754173182,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1791236337553,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In the GPU I diveded the componets based on their pupose. For compute we see various like:\n\n    - Streaming Multiprocessors (SMs): the core processing units of a GPU. Each SM contains multiple CUDA and\n        Tensor cores.\n    - CUDA Cores: deputed to perform general purpose operations \n    - Tensor Cores: specialized cores introduced in NVIDIA's Volta architecture, Tensor Cores accelerate matrix\n        operations crucial for deep learning.\n    - Shared Memory: a small, very fast memory local to the SM.\n    - Global Memory: the large GPU memory, much bigger but slower to access than shared memory.\n\nInside the GPU we also find a Video Random Access Memory (VRAM). This is the dedicated memory used by the\nGPU to store data and model parameters. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In the GPU I diveded the componets based on their pupose. For compute we see various like:\n\n    - Streaming Multiprocessors (SMs): the core processing units of a GPU. Each SM contains multiple CUDA and\n        Tensor cores.\n    - CUDA Cores: deputed to perform general purpose operations \n    - Tensor Cores: specialized cores introduced in NVIDIA's Volta architecture, Tensor Cores accelerate matrix\n        operations crucial for deep learning.\n    - Shared Memory: a small, very fast memory local to the SM.\n    - Global Memory: the large GPU memory, much bigger but slower to access than shared memory.\n\nInside the GPU we also find a Video Random Access Memory (VRAM). This is the dedicated memory used by the GPU to store data and model parameters. ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "created": 1791227280304,
      "labelPosition": null,
      "baseFontSize": null
    },
